# OutlastRetirement has no required environment variables. It's a
# client-only static app -- there's no server component, no database, and
# (as of the Live Pricing rework -- see README.md) no serverless function
# either.
#
# The premium Detailed Holdings tab's access token is verified entirely
# client-side against the public key baked into src/config/premiumPublicKey.js
# (see README.md's "Premium Access" section), and Live Pricing reads
# directly from each user's own Google Sheet (see README.md's "Live
# Pricing" section) -- neither needs a secret on your deployment.
#
# This file is kept only so `vercel env pull` / local tooling that expects
# a .env.example doesn't error on its absence. There's nothing to fill in.
